# Built from the teachings under "The gospel that must be believed" in studies/data/topics/salvation.json,
# with standalone teachings on the same theme. Slide text is the author's own sentences.

=== The gospel
# from 11402
--- The Gospel That Must Be Believed [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: The Gospel That Must Be Believed
sub: This is the Gospel. This is what one must believe to be saved.
refs: 1 Corinthians 15:1-4; Acts 16:31; John 3:16
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 11402, 16594
--- The gospel which I preached
kicker: The doctrine
scripture: 1 Corinthians 15:1-4 | mark: how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day
callout: If you don’t believe that you stand and are saved by the death, burial and resurrection of Christ Jesus, as foretold in scripture and witnessed by many, you aren’t saved.

# from 11402
--- What must I do to be saved?
lead: When the Philippian Jailer asks Paul and Silas, “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?” And they reply, “Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved,” this is what he had to believe.
big: Acts 16:31 | mark: Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved
p: That Jesus is the Christ. That by His death, our sins are forgiven, in His blood, and in His resurrection, the promise of eternal life.

# from 11404
--- What one must understand
lead: This is what one must understand to repent towards God and salvation in Christ Jesus.
- If you don’t believe you are a sinner, or that as a sinner you deserve Hell and death, you won’t accept the Gospel.
- If you don’t believe that salvation from the wages of your sin; Hell and death, is a free gift, given by God’s grace and not of yourself, you cannot turn to believe the Gospel.
- If you don’t believe that Jesus is the Son of God, Who was made flesh, lived a sinless life, was crucified, buried and risen again, that we may have remission of sin and eternal life, you can’t believe and be saved.
- If you think that anything you do can justify you, or to lose that free gift, given by God by grace through faith in Christ, you aren’t saved.
- If you don’t accept the gift from God in Jesus name, calling upon the name of the Lord to forgive you, a sinner, you cannot be saved.

=== John 3:16
# from 13452
--- The whole gospel
big: John 3:16
p: That’s it. That’s the entire good news of the living God by His grace, His **love** for the entire world, not some.
p: The Father gave His Son as a gift. Not to some. But to **whosoever**, without caveat or conditions except one, **that believes**.
callout: When someone is bringing doctrine to you that sounds ok or a little sus, and you’re just not sure if it’s right or not, compare it to [[John 3:16]]. If it violates any of it, you know immediately it’s a false gospel.

# from 13452, 16594
--- He that believeth is not condemned
scripture: John 3:17-18 | mark: He that believeth on him is not condemned
p: He that believes *not* is condemned. He that believes is not condemned. Repent and believe; Turn from non-believer to believer. That is the Gospel.
callout-honest: If you don’t know for sure you have eternal life, you don’t know the gospel and you aren’t saved. [[1 John 5:13]]

# from 8719, 13452
--- Faith is trusting God’s word
lead: Faith is trusting someone or something promised. Relying on the hope of an offer or covenant.
big: Romans 10:17
p: Faith in God relies on His word being true, His promises being kept. God, who cannot lie tells us His word, and by hearing, we believe the report. That is faith.
p: Believe means trust to be true. To have faith in. A secure knowledge. A lively hope. It doesn’t mean anything more than that.
note: It isn’t a mystical force. It isn’t will-to-power sorcery.

=== Saved by believing
# from 11402, 2657
--- The Ethiopian eunuch
scripture: Acts 8:35-37 | mark: If thou believest with all thine heart, thou mayest; I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God
p: The Gospel that was preached to the Ethiopian Eunuch was of Jesus being the Christ as promised in scripture. Not his willingness to turn from sin. Not his making Jesus “boss” of his life. Nothing about himself. Nothing more than accepting the truth about Jesus Christ.
callout: This is the order of things, and baptism is but a public expression of the salvation that came from belief.

# from 11407
--- Cornelius
scripture: Acts 10:43-44 | mark: whosoever believeth in him shall receive remission of sins
p: And, while still preaching Christ, they who heard believed and were not only saved, but bestowed gifts by the Holy Ghost.
p: Also note that their salvation and gifts came before being baptized. Not after or a result of.
note: Jesus Christ IS Lord of all. He doesn’t need you to anoint Him. God the Father already has. [[Acts 10:36]]

# from 11410
--- Jesus is the Christ
tile: Paul | [[Acts 9:20]]
tile: Peter | [[Matthew 16:16]]
tile: Andrew | [[John 1:41]]
tile: Thomas | [[John 20:28-29]]
p: We have example after example of those saved by faith on the risen Christ, who believed and it was counted unto them for righteousness. Not of repenting from sin. Not because they tried to avoid sin. Not because of anything of themselves, but the declaration that Jesus is Christ.

# from 11410
--- One apostle repented
lead: There is one apostle who repented, however.
lit: Judas repented himself | Matthew 27:3-5
p: And we know how that turned out for that reprobate.

=== One name, one gospel
# from 2510
--- None other name
big: Acts 4:12
p: It is in Jesus Christ’s name that we are saved, there is none who come to the Father except through the Son. There is no ecumenical path to heaven.
panel-warn: Not by other faiths | There are none saved by other faiths, trusting in their works, praying in the name of another.
panel: The Son | If you are looking for righteousness and truth, you cannot find it in anyone else or belief in any other power but that of the Son. The matchless name of Jesus Christ.

# from 17338
--- Calling upon the name of the Lord
big: Romans 10:13
panel-warn: Not this | Not “turning from your sins.” Calling upon the name of the Lord isn’t “asking Jesus into your heart.” It’s not giving your life to Jesus.
panel: But this | Admitting that you’re a sinner. It’s confessing He is the Christ. It’s knowing He gave His for you.

# from 12272, 11295
--- Plus nothing, minus nothing
panel-warn: Perishing | If you are trusting in anything other than the finished work of Christ to save you from Hell and death, if you are trusting in traditions, rites, your sacrifices, prayers to saints, carnal ordinances and sacraments, doing good works or turning from your sins to save you, you are assuredly perishing.
panel: The only salvation | The only salvation is by grace of God, the unmerited favor He extends to all, that whosoever believes on His Son, who was made flesh, lived a sinless life, died for our transgressions, suffered in our place, and rose again to life after 3 days and nights. Period. Plus nothing. Minus nothing.
callout: Anyone who adds requirements to this belief on Christ Jesus for salvation, in any manner, isn’t saved, and is bringing a false gospel. [[Galatians 1:8-9]]

